[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":11,"col":11},"end":{"line":11,"col":73}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`List.foldl` changes `Main.initial` in place, but it is `initial`, a top-level\nvalue.\n\n11|setup n = List.foldl [ n ] initial λvalue cells → List.set cells 0 value\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n7|initial = [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nBuild the value inside a function, so that each call makes fresh lists:\n\n    init ⊤ = …\n\nCall that function where the model is made. Wrapping `initial` in `λ⊤ → initial`\nstill returns the same shared value.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list. `init` builds its model; a top-level value it returns is still\nshared (ownership-checker.md §22.2)."}]
